 2025. He is not a member of the Executive Management.","context":"(6) Member of the restructuring committee constituted on June 20, 2024.","section":"ITEM 6. DIRECTORS, SENIOR MANAGEMENT AND EMPLOYEES","block":1500,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-035684","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-07-31","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001516899","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1516899/000149315226035684/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/a4bc0d9bb00b77dd50a28dc24785e4fa76cd12a6474951570c567165f42f6d9d.bin","sha256":"a4bc0d9bb00b77dd50a28dc24785e4fa76cd12a6474951570c567165f42f6d9d"}},{"id":"4118d239ac79b57a685417e13b2c5a580890a3cf42eb35a19bcf0d2270426eb4","quote":"Anuj Kumar Sethi. Mr. Sethi was appointed as Company’s Principal Financial Officer and Principal Accounting Officer effective from April 11, 2025. Mr. Sethi was Sr. Director Finance at CWT India Private Limited. He had worked with CWT India Private limited from April 2000 to December 2011. He has served as Chief Financial Officer of the Company in his earlier stint as well and has also served the Company for more than a decade in the senior finance and accounts role. He has completed his course from the Institute of Cost and Works Accountants of India and B. Com degree from Punjab University.","context":"Manish Amin. Mr. Amin is our Co-Founder and has served as our Chief Information and Technology Officer since January 2006. He also serves as a director of, Globe All India Services Limited, TSI Yatra Private Limited, and Yatra MICE and Holidays Limited (Formerly Yatra MICE and Holidays Private Limited) (Earlier Adventure and Nature Network Private Limited or ANN) which are subsidiaries of Yatra India and also serves as a Director of Middle East Travel Management Company Pvt. Ltd. Prior to joining our company, Mr. Amin worked at Ebookers, from June 1990 to November 2005 where his last role was Head of Technology Infrastructure. He holds a general certificate in business studies from South Thames College.","section":"ITEM 6. DIRECTORS, SENIOR MANAGEMENT AND EMPLOYEES","block":1508,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-035684","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-07-31","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001516899","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1516899/000149315226035684/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/a4bc0d9bb00b77dd50a28dc24785e4fa76cd12a6474951570c567165f42f6d9d.bin","sha256":"a4bc0d9bb00b77dd50a28dc24785e4fa76cd12a6474951570c567165f42f6d9d"}},{"id":"726ba27d8b757f42239d712fb8473b2ef2bd1fc99838165dd4d88c637adeeff8","quote":"Prior to this, he also led the successful integration of Abacus, a leading GDS in the Asia-Pacific region, which Sabre acquired in 2015. Under his leadership, Sabre’s business in the region significantly expanded through strategic customer wins and renewals. Prior to his executive position in Travel Network, Mr. Mendis served as president of Travelocity and Zuji, both consumer-facing brands that were part of the Sabre portfolio. Mr. Mendis also serves on the Board at Conferma Ltd. and was the first Chairman during the setting up of the Joint Venture business between Sabre Corporation and Mastercard Inc.","context":"Roshan Mendis. Mr. Mendis has served as a non-executive member of our Board since January 17, 2022. Mr. Mendis is currently serving as a CEO of a portfolio company for Insight Partners. Prior to that he was chief commercial officer and executive vice president of Travel Solutions at Sabre Corporation where he was is responsible for overseeing global commercial operations and business development for Sabre’s Travel Solutions customer portfolio - encompassing both agency and airline sales. In his previous role as chief commercial officer for Travel Network, Mr. Mendis built and developed a strong global team that oversaw sales activity for Sabre’s global agency customer base. Mr. Mendis currently serves as a board member of Yatra India","section":"ITEM 6. DIRECTORS, SENIOR MANAGEMENT AND EMPLOYEES","block":1514,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-035684","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-07-31","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001516899","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1516899/000149315226035684/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/a4bc0d9bb00b77dd50a28dc24785e4fa76cd12a6474951570c567165f42f6d9d.bin","sha256":"a4bc0d9bb00b77dd50a28dc24785e4fa76cd12a6474951570c567165f42f6d9d"}},{"id":"c56dc76fa43dda383ae5b6c5c70a19e675163723737e1cd03f668504e3e94e84","quote":"A native of Sri Lanka, Mr. Mendis completed his undergraduate studies at Chaminade University of Honolulu and University of Cambridge (UK). He later earned his MBA at the Rice University in Houston, Texas. Mr. Mendis was appointed to the Board pursuant to a Cooperation agreement, dated January 17, 2022.","context":"Prior to this, he also led the successful integration of Abacus, a leading GDS in the Asia-Pacific region, which Sabre acquired in 2015. Under his leadership, Sabre’s business in the region significantly expanded through strategic customer wins and renewals. Prior to his executive position in Travel Network, Mr. Mendis served as president of Travelocity and Zuji, both consumer-facing brands that were part of the Sabre portfolio. Mr. Mendis also serves on the Board at Conferma Ltd. and was the first Chairman during the setting up of the Joint Venture business between Sabre Corporation and Mastercard Inc.","section":"ITEM 6. DIRECTORS, SENIOR MANAGEMENT AND EMPLOYEES","block":1515,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-035684","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-07-31","reportDate":"2026-03-31","